    "title": "U.S. 29 Northbound lanes shut down in Madison County - NewsBreak",
    "text": "6 hours ago\nMadison County authorities announced late this afternoon that the northbound lanes of U.S. Route 29 at the intersection of Shelby Road is closed.\n“At approximately 3:30 p.m., a critical incident occurred in Madison County,” Madison County Administrator Jonathon Weakley reported in a press release.\nMadison County Sheriff’s Office also reports of a vehicular wreck on Rt. 29 North, just south of Wolftown-Hood Road.\n“Law enforcement is notifying the public that over the next several hours, Route 29 North will be closed at the intersection of Route 29 North and Shelby Road.” Virginia State Police and Virginia Department of Transportation are on scene to assist with the incident and rerouting of northbound traffic. Motorists should be advised of delays and plan their trip accordingly.\nThe post U.S. 29 Northbound lanes shut down in Madison County first appeared on The Piedmont Journal Recorder .\n2",
